+    /**
+     * Per-joint feedback reception statistics.
+     *
+     * PATCHED ADDITION (not present upstream).  The upstream class only exposes
+     * a sticky `feedbackReady()` boolean, which cannot distinguish "receiving
+     * continuously" from "stopped receiving after the first packet", and it
+     * exposes no reception timestamp at all.  These counters/timestamps let a
+     * caller detect stale feedback and stamp a state with the time the data
+     * actually arrived instead of the time it was read.
